{"reference":"Joshua 24","book":"Joshua","chapter":24,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Covenant at Shechem","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Joshua 24 centers on a covenant ceremony at Shechem. Joshua retells God’s actions for Israel, calls the people to serve God alone, records their commitment, and sets up a stone as a witness. The ceremony makes the people’s repeated choice and testimony public and memorable.","verse_refs":["Joshua 24:1-28"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_joshua_024_258e04d18001b840a8c6274c"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Book’s Movement","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Within the movement of Joshua, this chapter brings the story to covenant renewal. The book has moved through succession and entry into the land, campaigns, land allotment, tribal unity, and Joshua’s farewell; the gathering at Shechem provides its culminating renewal of commitment.","verse_refs":["Joshua 1","Joshua 10:1-43","Joshua 11:1-23","Joshua 12:1-24","Joshua 13:1-33","Joshua 14:1-15","Joshua 15:1-63","Joshua 16:1-10","Joshua 17:1-18","Joshua 18:1-28","Joshua 19:1-51","Joshua 20:1-9","Joshua 21:1-45","Joshua 22:1-34","Joshua 23:1-16","Joshua 2:1-24","Joshua 3:1-17","Joshua 4:1-24","Joshua 5:1-15","Joshua 6:1-27","Joshua 7:1-26","Joshua 8:1-35","Joshua 9:1-27"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_joshua_024_334f5fde51ea1a5663b4a55b"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}